{
  "_schema": "Data feed for the Express Insurance SEM dashboard live sections. Keys: _schema (this text). pmaxNote: string shown under the PMax ROAS KPI in the green KPI band. monthOrder: array of month labels shown in the Monthly dropdown, newest first. months: object keyed by month label; each month has periodLabel and compareLabel (display strings for the Performance section header), kpi (accountRoas, nonBrand, bestRoas, pmaxRoas: numbers; bestName: campaign name string; convValue: total conversion value in dollars; convValueNote: display string under the Total Conv. Value KPI), stats (impressions, clicks, conversions, convValue, cost, cpc; each is {v: number, chg: display change string like '+12.4%'}), campaigns (array in table order of {key, cost, conv, cpa, convValue, roas}; key is one of brand, pmax, pi, acct, pl, eng, dg; eng and dg carry paused: true and render as paused rows), geo (periodLabel display string plus locations: array of {name: bar label, tableName: table label, state, conv: conversions this period, prev: conversions previous period}). last30: same shape as a month entry, used for the Last 30 Days mode. custom: inputs for the Custom range mode; dailyRates are account-level per-day averages (impressions, clicks, conversions, convValue, cost), campaignDailyRates are per-day cost/conv/convValue per campaign key, geoDailyRates are per location {rate: conversions per day, tableName, state}, monthFactor maps 'YYYY-MM' to per-metric multipliers applied to the daily rates when aggregating a custom range (dates outside the listed months are clamped to the nearest listed month). Volume metrics scale with the number of days selected; deltas are computed against the previous equal-length window. | budget: array of {name,type,key,daily,monthly[,color]} for the Budget section (Looker/manual; subtext auto-formats as 'type \u2014 ROAS x.xx' using the campaign ROAS matched by key). commentary: {pmax, geo, landing:{headline,body}} manual (Kirsten). months[m] may also carry assetGroups: array of {name,spend,conv,convValue,roas} (Google Ads) and its own budget/commentary/lob overrides. lob: array of {n,r,t} overriding the LTV revenue defaults (Looker).",
